={
  "visitSchedule": "Subjects will participate in five scheduled study visits over a 12-week period. These will include a screening/baseline visit, two interim follow-up visits at Week 4 and Week 8, a final evaluation at Week 12, and an exit visit if subjects discontinue prematurely. The visit schedule, complete with visit windows and associated CRF forms, is summarized in the table below. Details of each visit, including the specific testing to be conducted, are provided in subsections 9.2.1 through 9.2.5.",
  "visitScheduleDetails": "9.2.1. Screening/Baseline\nAt the baseline visit, subjects will undergo informed consent, eligibility confirmation, assignment of study ID, and collection of demographic and medical history. Baseline assessments will include vital signs (blood pressure, heart rate), complete blood count, serum electrolytes, liver function tests, ECG, and quality of life questionnaire.\n\n9.2.2. Week 4 Follow-up\nSubjects will return for interim evaluation at Week 4 (±7 days). Assessments will include vital signs (blood pressure, heart rate) and monitoring for treatment-emergent adverse events. Compliance with study medication will also be reviewed.\n\n9.2.3. Week 8 Follow-up\nAt Week 8 (±7 days), subjects will undergo vital signs measurement and review of adverse events. Ongoing medication compliance and safety will be evaluated.\n\n9.2.4. Week 12 Final Visit\nAt Week 12 (±7 days), subjects will undergo final efficacy and safety evaluations. Assessments will include vital signs (blood pressure, heart rate), complete blood count, serum electrolytes, liver function tests, ECG, and quality of life questionnaire. Adverse events and medication compliance will also be recorded.\n\n9.2.5. Exit Procedures\nSubjects who discontinue early will complete an exit visit as soon as possible. The exit visit will include safety evaluations, vital signs, review of adverse events, and return of study medication where applicable.",
