  "measurements": "All routine testing and planned study assessments will be conducted at each scheduled visit. Any abnormalities identified should be documented in the CRF 'Comment' section. Specific study examination procedures are outlined below.",
  "measurementsDetails": "9.3.1. Vital Signs\nBlood pressure and heart rate will be measured at each scheduled visit (baseline, week 4, week 8, week 12) using a calibrated sphygmomanometer. Measurements will be taken in a seated position after a minimum of 5 minutes rest.\n\n9.3.2. Laboratory Testing\nComplete blood count, serum electrolytes, and liver function tests will be performed at baseline and week 12. Samples will be collected via venipuncture and analyzed at a certified central laboratory.\n\n9.3.3. ECG\nA standard 12-lead electrocardiogram will be conducted at baseline and week 12. ECGs will be evaluated for any clinically significant abnormalities by a blinded cardiologist.\n\n9.3.4. Quality of Life Questionnaire\nA validated hypertension-specific quality of life instrument will be administered at baseline and week 12. Questionnaires will be completed by subjects under the supervision of site personnel to ensure completeness and accuracy.",
  "startDate": "2025-06-01",
  "endDate": "2027-03-31"
}

